# Scientific evidence and reproduction

Both personal arguments have separate sealed PRE and POST comparisons. The
original Part II checker confirms its affected final publication source. A
separate recovery checker reviews the full released publication and its joins
after the earlier review was interrupted. These final comparisons reuse
explicitly bound evidence; neither is another blind derivation or an approval
from the interrupted Part I checker. Its partial work remains preserved.
The root read the arguments, new checker code, compact outputs and failure
records and freshly replayed read-only evidence checks.

During the recovery review, 57 already captured files in the original Part II
final comparison were sealed concurrently. The first preservation check
stopped on chmod/ctime changes; the second permits exactly those metadata
changes, preserving all original bytes. The failed attempt and exception are
recorded. The root's later replay preserved all 689 observed files in both
bytes and metadata and reproduced the full recovery output exactly.

The canonical runner executes exact copies of both personally sealed programs.
The fresh current result matches all177399 non-timing leaves and the support
result all249500. Only elapsed times differ. No finite-time numerical
propagation or laboratory fit was run by the canonical runner.

POST46 corrected a false exclusivity in prose about vanishing Hamiltonian
current on zero-field inputs. The separate qualified copy removes only that
exclusivity. Original proofs and sealed histories remain unchanged. PRE47's
formation-factor remainder and Pearson normalization remain separately
attributed; they are not the personal all-time bound or Cov/Var quotient.

Historical writers and absolute paths are evidence, not the portable entry
point. Duplicate snapshots, generated binaries and historical whitespace diffs
are retained externally with explicit bindings. Large byte-identical artifacts
are included once with duplicate mappings. No inherited private-branch data or
third-party extracts are included.

A graph-manifest write was attempted before its producer finished. It failed
on the missing graph; the freeze verifier then rejected the unchanged base
manifest. Neither wrote its target record. That bookkeeping failure and the
prior verifier are preserved. The later complete generation is verified.
